// Certificates as a server presents them and a client judges them:
// the system's trust anchors, an identity per name chosen by SNI, a
// wildcard served through an intermediate, an address checked as an
// address, and the refusals verification owes — a chain missing its
// intermediate, an expired leaf, a wildcard asked to cover two labels,
// a client that names no host. The fixtures below are signed by the
// test authority in @std.tls.testing and are good for nothing else.
use @std.io.{read_bytes}
use @std.tls.{Config, TlsError, client, server, anchored, roots_path}
use @std.tls.testing.{localhost_ca, localhost_chain, localhost_key, trusting_localhost}

